# Block30 preflight witnesses

Work in displacement units with old axial centers `0,f,2f,3f` and Block28
outputs `A=f+g`, `B=2f+h`.

For `g=h`, the displayed words end at `f+3g` and `2f+3g`, with fronts `f`
and `-f`.  For `g` perpendicular to `h`, they end at `2f+g+h` and
`f+g+h`; after reordering, the fronts point inward.  For `h=-g`, both
chirality words end at `f+s(f cross g)` and `2f+s(f cross g)`, again with
inward fronts.

An ephemeral preflight exhausted 192 frame/chirality cases, 4,608 proper-
rotation transports, and 192 side exchanges.  It found lawful non-reversing
straight/perpendicular steps, distinct fresh centers, disjoint arms, and
returned-facing endpoints in every case.  These numbers are preflight only;
the target runner must recompute them from the formulas.

The two signs in the opposite orbit are physically distinct under the named
symmetry: proper rotations preserve the cross-product sign and side exchange
maps `(-f,-g)` back to the same `f cross g`.  Only an improper reflection
interchanges them, and improper reflections are not part of the supplied
Lattice symmetry.
